"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "enpe7n4le03ob08re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}]}], "id": 0}], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Java virtual machine", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}, {"contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}], "type": "learning_skills"}], "id": 11, "type": "DWS"}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "text": "<strong>Michelle:</strong> Danny, I need your help! I didn't come to class! Could you help me?</br>\n<strong>Danny:</strong> Sure! We read everything about Java. You may be confused if you come to class tomorrow without things clear. Let me try to recap everything so you can take notes!</br>\n<strong>Michelle:</strong> That'd be great! I heard Laura was so bewildered by it that I'm pretty sure it must be very difficult! </br>\n<strong>Danny:</strong> We'll see! Let's start by defining some basic concepts. Do you know what a code is?</br>", "id": 0, "image": "enpe7n4le03ob08re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "32000", "text": "<strong>Michelle:</strong> A code is something we use to allude to the statements that we write in a programming language.</br>\n<strong>Danny:</strong> Well, you must have some basic concepts clear, so let's move on to Java's definition. Java is a general-purpose computer programming. We consider it as an object-oriented program, which means that we might create programs constructed in Java in terms of objects. Likewise, we see it as a generic program and its platform supports concurrent programming. Now, you might want to know how it works. Java works with a platform-independence since it manages to reorganize the compile-link-execute sequence. Remember that the compiler is the one in charge of turning the statements you wrote in a language into codes. With this implementation, developers succeeded in isolating the dependent issues. </br>", "id": 1, "image": "enpe7n4le03ob08re2img02.jpg"}, {"time": "91000", "text": "Thus, its compiler, well-known as JVM compiler, creates a bytecode which is an object file that works for a virtual machine. Each platform has a Java interpreter that links to a specific code. Compiling this bytecode may help you get Java programs to be faster\u2026 Well, after this explanation you can't feel as lost as you were before! You could be confused, but you will get it!! </br>\n<strong>Michelle</strong>: Thanks Danny! Of course, I'm not confused now! You could be a great teacher! However\u2026 why don't we talk about it one more time?", "id": 2, "image": "enpe7n4le03ob08re2img03.jpg"}], "coverimg": "enpe7n4le03ob08re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n4le03ob08re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "title": "", "id": 1, "type": "audio"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "contents": [{"value": "<strong>Michelle:</strong> Danny, I need your help! I didn't come to class! Could you help me?</br>\n<strong>Danny:</strong> Sure! We read everything about Java. You may be confused if you come to class tomorrow without things clear. Let me try to recap everything so you can take notes!</br>\n<strong>Michelle:</strong> That'd be great! I heard Laura was so bewildered by it that I'm pretty sure it must be very difficult! </br>\n<strong>Danny:</strong> We'll see! Let's start by defining some basic concepts. Do you know what a code is?</br>\n<strong>Michelle:</strong> A code is something we use to allude to the statements that we write in a programming language.</br>\n<strong>Danny:</strong> Well, you must have some basic concepts clear, so let's move on to Java's definition. Java is a general-purpose computer programming. We consider it as an object-oriented program, which means that we might create programs constructed in Java in terms of objects. Likewise, we see it as a generic program and its platform supports concurrent programming. Now, you might want to know how it works. Java works with a platform-independence since it manages to reorganize the compile-link-execute sequence. Remember that the compiler is the one in charge of turning the statements you wrote in a language into codes. With this implementation, developers succeeded in isolating the dependent issues. </br>\nThus, its compiler, well-known as JVM compiler, creates a bytecode which is an object file that works for a virtual machine. Each platform has a Java interpreter that links to a specific code. Compiling this bytecode may help you get Java programs to be faster\u2026 Well, after this explanation you can't feel as lost as you were before! You could be confused, but you will get it!! </br>\n<strong>Michelle</strong>: Thanks Danny! Of course, I'm not confused now! You could be a great teacher! However\u2026 why don't we talk about it one more time?", "type": "p"}], "title": "", "id": 2, "type": "static"}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar"}], "type": "sena"}